Since I was working with a simple map structure, toObject saved me... e.g.

```
var MyComponent = React.createClass({
  mixins: [PureRenderMixin],
  getInitialState(){
    return MyStore.getState().toObject(); //getState returns a Immutable.Map()
  },
  ...
});
```

Not sure how well this work with more complex object structures however.
